  <p>This is a topic of heated dabate because to encrypt a seed phrase you need to enter it into a computer, phone, or some digital device. On one side are the people who follow the mantra of not entering a seed phrase into a device that is not their hardware wallet. On the other hand the poeple who say if the device is secure and offline then what is the problem. I'm not going to take a side, I think each makes good points. However, there is a way to encrypt a seedphrase without entering it into a device at all. In fact you can do it completely by hand without any crazy complex math just some bitwise operations.</p>

